# HELM design system

Official identity: **HELM | حِلْم**. Preserve that Arabic spelling, including the kasra.

The Arabic wordmark is custom, refined Naskh-inspired calligraphy with visible تشكيل. IBM Plex Sans Arabic is the Arabic interface font. Do not present it, or any other generic Arabic UI font, as the finished wordmark. Until an approved wordmark asset is in the repo, render accessible temporary text with the exact spelling. Do not generate or invent a logo.

## Color

Approved Phase 1A traveler Flutter palette:

Light (luxury editorial):

- Background `#F7F4ED`
- Surface `#FFFFFF`
- Sand `#E5DED2`
- Primary `#173D35`
- Sage `#789D8C` — decorative accent only
- Champagne `#BCA47E` — tertiary fill only

Dark (cinematic):

- Background `#0B151C`
- Surface `#142831`
- Selected surface `#24534F`
- Primary `#68B5A5`
- Text `#F3EFE6`
- Muted text `#A6C0BC`

Brand colors are not interchangeable foregrounds and backgrounds. Text, focus, control boundaries, and interactive states must meet WCAG on the surface they actually sit on.

Approved contrast (approximate):

- Primary on light background: about 10.89:1. Body text.
- Primary on white surface: about 11.96:1. Body text.
- White / light surface on primary: about 11.96:1. Primary control labels.
- Dark text on dark background: about 16.08:1. Body text.
- Dark muted on dark surface: about 7.90:1. Secondary text.
- Dark primary on dark background: about 7.68:1. Accent and focus.
- Sage on white: about 3.00:1. Insufficient for text or reliable non-text UI. Decorative only.
- Champagne on light background: about 2.18:1. Insufficient as text or boundary. Use primary labels on champagne fills.
- Dark muted on selected surface: about 4.49:1. Insufficient for AA body text — do not place muted copy on selected surfaces.

Flutter maps these into `ColorScheme` in `HelmTheme`. Legacy token names (`ivory`, `midnight`, `deepOcean`, `teal`, `coral`) remain as aliases onto Phase 1A values for existing call sites.

Semantic error and success colors stay non-brand Material-style roles (`HelmErrorColors`, `HelmSuccessColors`) with AA contrast on Phase 1A surfaces. A new semantic danger, success, or neutral convention still needs review before it becomes a broader visual rule.

## Type

- English headings: Fraunces — page 32, section 24, card 20 dp.
- English UI and body: Outfit — body 16 / 14, actions 14, metadata 12 dp.
- Arabic UI: IBM Plex Sans Arabic.
- Arabic branding: the separate Naskh-inspired wordmark.

Arabic runs use `lang="ar"` and RTL direction. Keep diacritics visible and line spacing comfortable. Keep decorative calligraphy off long-form Arabic interface copy.

## Spacing

Approved scale: 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48 dp. Standard screen padding: 20 dp (`HelmSpacing.screen`). Soft radii remain 8 / 12 / 16 / 24 (sheet).

## Components and styling

Use soft, refined radii on buttons, cards, inputs, and bottom sheets. Every interactive control has a clear primary, secondary, disabled, loading, hover, and focus treatment. Traveler surfaces stay spacious. Admin stays denser and still accessible.

Share token names across Next.js and Flutter. Implement them in the platform's current system:

- Traveler web: existing global CSS (not yet migrated to Phase 1A).
- Admin: existing CSS Modules and global tokens (not yet migrated to Phase 1A).
- Flutter: `ThemeData` and reusable widgets (`HelmColors`, `HelmTheme`, `HelmTokens`, `HelmTypography`).

Do not add a styling library, UI package, or design dependency without separate approval.

## Imagery and invented data

Use destination photography only when published data supplies a resolvable image URL and alt text. When an image is unavailable, use a deliberate text presentation and omit the image frame. Do not invent images, prices, ratings, availability, or booking states.
